Rem ==========================================
Rem   BASIC JIT - Command Reference & Examples
Rem ==========================================
Rem
Rem  Use "Rem" to write comments (ignored by compiler)
Rem  Run this file:  ./build/release/bin/basicjit example.basic


Rem ==========================================
Rem  1. PRINT - Display output
Rem ==========================================

Print "Hello, World!"
Print 42
Print "Score: "; 100                   : Rem semicolon keeps items on same line
Print "Line 1" : Print "Line 2"        : Rem colon separates statements on one line
Print ""                                : Rem prints a blank line


Rem ==========================================
Rem  2. VARIABLES - Three types
Rem ==========================================

Rem  Integer (ends with %)
age% = 21
count% = 0

Rem  Float/Double (no suffix)
pi = 3.14159
temperature = 98.6

Rem  Boolean (ends with ?)
isReady? = True
isDone? = False

Rem  String (ends with $)
name$ = "Abhishek"

Print "Name: "; name$
Print "Age: "; age
Print "Pi: "; pi
Print "Ready? "; isReady


Rem ==========================================
Rem  3. ARITHMETIC - Math operators
Rem ==========================================

A% = 20
B% = 7

Print "20 + 7  = "; A + B              : Rem Addition
Print "20 - 7  = "; A - B              : Rem Subtraction
Print "20 * 7  = "; A * B              : Rem Multiplication
Print "20 / 7  = "; A / B              : Rem Integer division
Print "20 Mod 7= "; A Mod B            : Rem Remainder
Print "2 ^ 8   = "; 2 ^ 8              : Rem Power


Rem ==========================================
Rem  4. MATH FUNCTIONS - Built-in
Rem ==========================================

Print "Abs(-5)    = "; Abs(-5)          : Rem Absolute value
Print "Sqr(25)    = "; Sqr(25)          : Rem Square root
Print "Int(3.9)   = "; Int(3.9)         : Rem Floor / truncate
Print "Sin(1.57)  = "; Sin(1.57)        : Rem Sine (radians)
Print "Cos(0)     = "; Cos(0)           : Rem Cosine
Print "Exp(1)     = "; Exp(1)           : Rem e^x
Print "Log(100)   = "; Log(100)         : Rem Natural log


Rem ==========================================
Rem  5. STRING FUNCTIONS - Built-in
Rem ==========================================

Print "Len(Hello)       = "; Len("Hello")
Print "Left(Hello, 3)   = "; Left("Hello", 3)
Print "Right(Hello, 3)  = "; Right("Hello", 3)
Print "Asc(A)           = "; Asc("A")         : Rem ASCII code
Print "Chr(90)          = "; Chr(90)           : Rem Character from code
Print "Concat            = "; "Hi" + " " + "there"


Rem ==========================================
Rem  6. IF / THEN / ELSE - Conditionals
Rem ==========================================

score% = 75

If score >= 90 Then Print "Grade: A"
If score >= 80 Then Print "Grade: B"
If score >= 70 Then Print "Grade: C"

Rem  Single-line IF/ELSE:
If score >= 80 Then Print "Pass with merit" Else Print "Pass"


Rem ==========================================
Rem  7. FOR / NEXT - Counted loops
Rem ==========================================

Rem  Basic loop: 1 to 5
Print "Count 1-5: ";
For I = 1 To 5
    Print I; " ";
Next I
Print ""

Rem  Loop with STEP
Print "Even numbers: ";
For I = 2 To 10 Step 2
    Print I; " ";
Next I
Print ""

Rem  Countdown with negative step
Print "Countdown: ";
For I = 5 To 1 Step -1
    Print I; " ";
Next I
Print "Go!"


Rem ==========================================
Rem  8. BOOLEAN LOGIC - And, Or, Not, Xor
Rem ==========================================

P? = True
Q? = False

Print "True And False = "; P And Q
Print "True Or  False = "; P Or Q
Print "Not True       = "; Not P
Print "True Xor False = "; P Xor Q


Rem ==========================================
Rem  9. DEF FN - User-defined functions
Rem ==========================================

Rem  Simple function
Def Fn double(X) = X * 2
Print "double(7) = "; Fn double(7)

Rem  Two parameters
Def Fn addNum(X, Y) = X + Y
Print "add(3,4)  = "; Fn addNum(3, 4)

Rem  Recursive function (Fibonacci)
Def Fn fib%(N%) = (If N <= 1 Then N Else Fn fib(N - 1) + Fn fib(N - 2))
Print "fib(10)   = "; Fn fib(10)


Rem ==========================================
Rem  10. DATA / READ - Stored data
Rem ==========================================

Data 10, 20, 30, 40, 50
Read V%, W%, X%, Y%, Z%
Print "Data values: "; V; " "; W; " "; X; " "; Y; " "; Z


Rem ==========================================
Rem  11. GOSUB / RETURN - Subroutines
Rem ==========================================

Print "Before subroutine"
GoSub mySubroutine
Print "After subroutine"
GoTo endProgram

mySubroutine:
    Print "  >> Inside subroutine!"
Return

endProgram:


Rem ==========================================
Rem  12. GOTO - Jump to a label
Rem ==========================================

GoTo skipThis
Print "You will never see this!"
skipThis:
Print "Jumped over the hidden message."


Rem ==========================================
Rem  Done!
Rem ==========================================
Print ""
Print "=== Example Complete ==="
